For some reason the FlexSPI driver does not live in RAM by default, it lives in wherever
your .text section is stored. This makes it impossible to use the driver when running XiP.
I think NXP expects you to fix this at the linker script level, but even their own default
linker script doesn't do this (???). This has been complained about on the forums too:
https://community.nxp.com/t5/i-MX-RT-Crossover-MCUs/Hard-Bus-Fault-while-running-AN12255SW-flash-remap-test/m-p/2032657#M33282

To fix this properly, we wrap each non-inline driver function in AT_QUICKACCESS_SECTION_CODE().
Then, for inline functions, we hit them with the force_inline attribute to make sure that if whatever
calls them is in RAM, they will be in RAM too.

